  {
   "id": "concept-serial",
   "label": "Serial and Parallel",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Serial and Parallel</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">The same letter, A (01000001 in ASCII), sent two ways.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 420 110\" width=\"420\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Serial: the 8 bits of A travel one after another down one wire\"><rect x=\"4\" y=\"30\" width=\"70\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"39\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">Sender</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"30\" width=\"70\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"381\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">Receiver</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"107\" cy=\"60\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107\" y=\"64.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><circle cx=\"136\" cy=\"60\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--warn, #fdd663)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"136\" y=\"64.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--warn, #fdd663)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">1</text><circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"60\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"165\" y=\"64.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><circle cx=\"194\" cy=\"60\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"194\" y=\"64.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><circle cx=\"223\" cy=\"60\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"223\" y=\"64.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><circle cx=\"252\" cy=\"60\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"252\" y=\"64.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><circle cx=\"281\" cy=\"60\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"281\" y=\"64.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"60\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--warn, #fdd663)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"64.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--warn, #fdd663)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">1</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">1 wire: one bit after another</text></svg><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Serial:</strong> one bit at a time, down a single wire.</li><li>The bits arrive in order, so it is reliable over long distances.</li><li>Fewer wires, so it is cheaper. But it is slower.</li></ul></div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 420 230\" width=\"420\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Parallel: the 8 bits of A travel side by side down eight wires\"><rect x=\"4\" y=\"30\" width=\"70\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"39\" y=\"133\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">Sender</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"30\" width=\"70\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"381\" y=\"133\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">Receiver</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"44\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"44\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"48.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"68\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"68\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--warn, #fdd663)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"72.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--warn, #fdd663)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">1</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"92\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"96.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"116\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"116\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"120.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"140\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"144.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"164\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"164\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"164\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"168.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"188\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"188\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"192.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">0</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"212\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"212\" stroke=\"var(--line-strong, #3b424e)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"212\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--warn, #fdd663)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"216.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--warn, #fdd663)\" font-family=\"ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace\">1</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">8 wires: all 8 bits at the same time</text></svg><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Parallel:</strong> several bits at the same time, down several wires.</li><li>Faster than serial.</li><li>Over a long distance the bits can <strong>skew</strong> (arrive out of step), so the data can be wrong. Short distances only.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-methods",
   "label": "Exam Question: Methods of Transmission",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y10-21l2-exam-methods",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Methods of Transmission</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/12, June 2024, Question 2(a). Data can be transmitted from one device to another.</p><div id=\"y10-21l2-exam-methods\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "Which term is not a method for transmitting data? [1]",
     "options": [
      "Serial",
      "Simplex",
      "Parity",
      "Parallel"
     ],
     "correct": 2,
     "explain": "Parity is a way of checking for errors. Serial, parallel and simplex are all methods of transmitting data."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "check-serial",
   "label": "Check: Serial or Parallel?",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y10-21l2-check-serial",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Serial or Parallel?</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Use the slide on serial and parallel.</p><div id=\"y10-21l2-check-serial\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "Which method sends several bits at the same time?",
     "options": [
      "Serial",
      "Parallel",
      "Simplex"
     ],
     "correct": 1,
     "explain": "Parallel sends several bits at once, one down each wire."
    },
    {
     "prompt": "Why is parallel not used over long distances?",
     "options": [
      "Its bits can skew and arrive out of step",
      "It only has one wire",
      "It is slower than serial"
     ],
     "correct": 0,
     "explain": "Over a long distance the wires are not all the same speed, so the bits skew."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "activity-1",
   "label": "Activity 1: Serial and Parallel",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "transmission-lab-wires",
   "embedContainerId": "y10-21l2-activity-1",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Activity 1: Serial and Parallel</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Send the letter both ways, down a short and a long cable. Complete the five tasks.</p><div id=\"y10-21l2-activity-1\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-serial",
   "label": "Exam Question: Why Serial?",
   "type": "self-marked-response",
   "containerId": "y10-21l2-exam-serial",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Why Serial?</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/12, March 2021, Question 1(d)(i). Electronic data about the final score for a hockey match is transmitted to a central computer 30 kilometres away, using serial transmission.</p><div id=\"y10-21l2-exam-serial\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "why-serial",
     "prompt": "Explain why serial transmission is more appropriate than parallel transmission in this scenario. [3]",
     "marks": 3,
     "modelAnswer": "Any three: the data travels a long distance (30 km); parallel bits could skew / arrive out of sync over that distance, so the data could be corrupted; serial sends one bit at a time, so the bits arrive in order and there are fewer errors; serial needs fewer wires, so it is cheaper over a long distance."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-umar",
   "label": "Exam Question: Parallel Simplex",
   "type": "self-marked-response",
   "containerId": "y10-21l2-exam-umar",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Parallel Simplex</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/13, June 2022, Question 7(b). Umar sends data from his computer to a file server using parallel simplex data transmission. The file server is moved to another building that is 1 km away.</p><div id=\"y10-21l2-exam-umar\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "umar-b",
     "prompt": "Explain why the parallel simplex data transmission method that Umar uses is no longer suitable. [2]",
     "marks": 2,
     "modelAnswer": "Any two: 1 km is a long distance for parallel; the bits could skew / arrive out of sync, so the data could be corrupted or have errors; many wires over 1 km would be expensive."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "concept-duplex",
   "label": "Simplex, Half-Duplex and Full-Duplex",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Simplex, Half-Duplex and Full-Duplex</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">These describe which way the data can travel.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 250\" width=\"460\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Simplex: A to B only. Half-duplex: both ways, one at a time. Full-duplex: both ways at once.\"><defs><marker id=\"y10-21l2-ah-a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\"/></marker><marker id=\"y10-21l2-ah-b\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#c58af9\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"0\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">Simplex</text><rect x=\"108\" y=\"18\" width=\"52\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"134\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">A</text><rect x=\"404\" y=\"18\" width=\"52\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">B</text><line x1=\"162\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#y10-21l2-ah-a)\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">Half-duplex</text><rect x=\"108\" y=\"100\" width=\"52\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"134\" y=\"127\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">A</text><rect x=\"404\" y=\"100\" width=\"52\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"127\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">B</text><line x1=\"164\" y1=\"122\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"122\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#y10-21l2-ah-a)\" marker-start=\"url(#y10-21l2-ah-a)\"/><text x=\"282\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">one direction at a time</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">Full-duplex</text><rect x=\"108\" y=\"182\" width=\"52\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"134\" y=\"209\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">A</text><rect x=\"404\" y=\"182\" width=\"52\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"var(--surface-2, #1d2128)\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"209\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"var(--ink, #e8eaed)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">B</text><line x1=\"162\" y1=\"194\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"194\" stroke=\"var(--brand, #8ab4f8)\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#y10-21l2-ah-a)\"/><line x1=\"400\" y1=\"214\" x2=\"164\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#c58af9\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#y10-21l2-ah-b)\"/><text x=\"282\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"var(--muted, #9aa0a6)\" font-family=\"Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif\">both directions at the same time</text></svg></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Simplex:</strong> one direction only. The receiver cannot send back.</li><li><strong>Half-duplex:</strong> both directions, but only one direction at a time.</li><li><strong>Full-duplex:</strong> both directions at the same time. Fastest for two-way data, but needs a channel each way.</li><li>A method has two parts, for example <strong>serial full-duplex</strong>.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
