  {
   "id": "exam-restaurant",
   "label": "Exam Question: Choosing a Method (1 of 2)",
   "type": "self-marked-response",
   "containerId": "y10-21l2-exam-restaurant",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Choosing a Method (1 of 2)</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/11, June 2025, Question 4(a)(i). A restaurant's ordering system transmits each customer's order across its network to a computer in the kitchen. The data is sent using serial full-duplex data transmission.</p><div id=\"y10-21l2-exam-restaurant\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "restaurant-i",
     "prompt": "Give two reasons why serial full-duplex is a suitable data transmission method for the data. [2]",
     "marks": 2,
     "modelAnswer": "Any two: data can be sent and received at the same time (for example the order goes to the kitchen while a confirmation comes back); serial is reliable over the distance to the kitchen, as the bits arrive in order and do not skew; serial needs fewer wires, so it is cheaper."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-restaurant-2",
   "label": "Exam Question: Choosing a Method (2 of 2)",
   "type": "self-marked-response",
   "containerId": "y10-21l2-exam-restaurant-2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Choosing a Method (2 of 2)</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/11, June 2025, Question 4(a)(ii). The restaurant considers parallel transmission instead of serial transmission.</p><div id=\"y10-21l2-exam-restaurant-2\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "restaurant-ii",
     "prompt": "Give one improvement that would be made to the data transmission if parallel transmission is used instead of serial transmission. [1]",
     "marks": 1,
     "modelAnswer": "The data would be transmitted faster."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "practice",
   "label": "Checked Practice",
